    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0142" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1894Nicaragua/pg135"/>

                <head>No. 83.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Herbert to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July 27,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith copies
                    of four communications, with inclosures, Nos. 4248, 4250, 4273, 4275, received
                    from Commander Charles O’Neil, U, S. N., commanding the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Marblehead</hi>, relative to political affairs in
                    Nicaragua.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. A. Herbert.</hi></signed></closer>

















